/**
 * @mainpage cpp-remote-profiler
 *
 * @section intro Introduction
 *
 * cpp-remote-profiler is a C++ remote profiling library similar to Go pprof and
 * the brpc pprof service. It embeds HTTP endpoints into the profiled process so
 * that CPU and heap profiles can be collected remotely and rendered directly as
 * flame-graph SVG.
 *
 * The profiling core is built on gperftools. The web layer is based on Drogon and
 * is @b optional: @c profiler_core has no web-framework dependency at all.
 *
 * @section features Features
 *
 * - @b CPU @b Profiling via gperftools sampling
 * - @b Heap @b Profiling with allocation analysis and leak detection
 * - @b Heap @b Growth @b Profiling (no @c TCMALLOC_SAMPLE_PARAMETER required)
 * - @b Thread @b Stack @b Capture across all threads
 * - @b Standard @b pprof @b Interface compatible with the Go pprof toolchain
 * - @b Framework @b Agnostic: @c ProfilerHttpHandlers return a plain response struct
 * - @b Optional @b Web @b Layer: a Drogon adapter is provided, others are supported
 * - @b Configurable @b Logging through the @c LogSink interface
 *
 * @section getting_started Quick Example
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * #include "profiler_manager.h"
 * #include "profiler/drogon_adapter.h"
 * #include <drogon/drogon.h>
 *
 * int main() {
 *     profiler::ProfilerManager profiler;
 *     profiler::registerDrogonHandlers(profiler);
 *     drogon::app().addListener("0.0.0.0", 8080).run();
 *     return 0;
 * }
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section api_endpoints API Endpoints
 *
 * The canonical, always-current endpoint list lives in the project README under
 * "API 端点" (README.md). Summary:
 *
 * - Standard pprof: @c /pprof/profile, @c /pprof/heap, @c /pprof/growth, @c /pprof/symbol
 * - One-click analysis (SVG): @c /api/{cpu,heap,growth}/analyze
 * - Raw SVG download: @c /api/{cpu,heap,growth}/svg_raw and @c .../flamegraph_raw
 * - Thread stacks: @c /api/thread/stacks
 * - Panel and viewers: @c /, @c /show_svg.html, @c /show_heap_svg.html, @c /show_growth_svg.html
 *
 * @section runtime_dependencies Runtime Dependencies
 *
 * @c ProfilerManager writes the @c pprof and @c flamegraph.pl Perl scripts into the
 * process working directory on construction and invokes them with relative paths.
 * The working directory must therefore be writable, and @c perl must be installed.
 *
 * @section installation Installation and Documentation
 *
 * Build instructions and the full user guide are in the repository:
 * README.md (build, endpoints, configuration),
 * docs/user_guide/02_api_reference.md (API reference),
 * docs/user_guide/05_installation.md (installation methods).
 *
 * @section license License
 *
 * MIT License
 *
 * @section links Links
 *
 * - GitHub: https://github.com/IronsDu/cpp-remote-profiler
 * - Issue Tracker: https://github.com/IronsDu/cpp-remote-profiler/issues
 */
